      "body": "## Overview\n\nAdd RedHatAI checkpoint variants to the existing Qwen3.8 recipes.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Covers Qwen3.8-27B, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, and Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B.\n- Keeps existing default checkpoints unchanged.\n- Marks estimated large-checkpoint VRAM values as estimates pending exact shard-size inspection.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidation is pending; this PR is intentionally a draft.\n\n- Passed: `git diff --check`.\n- Planned source validation (not run): from `/home/Roderick-Wu/recipes`, run `pnpm install` if dependencies are missing, then:\n  `node scripts/validate-source.mjs --source vllm --dir /home/Roderick-Wu/recipe-worktrees/qwen38/recipes`\n- These added NVFP4 variants are Blackwell-labeled and cannot be serving-tested on the available 8xH100 node. Run the generated serving command on supported Blackwell hardware before marking ready.\n\n## Details\n\nQwen3.8-Flash-Next has a separate open PR, [#63755](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63755), for a RadixArk NVFP4 profile on RTX PRO 6000. This change adds the distinct RedHatAI checkpoint variant. AI assistance was used to prepare this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] Design Fit: confines changes to existing recipe files and preserves defaults.\n- [ ] Testing and Validation: pending source validation and Blackwell serving test.\n- [x] Code Quality and Style: `git diff --check` passed.\n- [x] Pull Request Contents: identifies estimates, hardware limits, and related PR #63755.\n</details>\n\n",
